{
  "_readme": [
    "Wend's single translation catalogue. Both the browser app and the",
    "server-rendered visitor pages read this file, so every word the product",
    "says lives here and nowhere else.",
    "",
    "Each entry is an object of language codes: 'en' is the source, the others",
    "are translations. To review a translation, read down the pairs — the",
    "English is always right next to it.",
    "",
    "Placeholders are written {like_this} and must survive translation intact,",
    "spelling included. They are substituted at runtime.",
    "",
    "The active language is chosen once, at deploy time, with CG_LANG in the",
    "environment (en | fr). There is no per-user language switch.",
    "",
    "Sections:",
    "  app     - the signed-in interface (React)",
    "  errors  - what the API says back when something is refused; keyed by",
    "            the English message so the Go call sites stay readable",
    "  visitor - the pages a person who clicks a short link can land on",
    "  months  - month names for the one date the server formats itself"
  ],
  "languages": [
    "en",
    "fr"
  ],
